    "answerHtml": "\n<div class=\"space-y-2.5 font-sans text-xs\">\n  <div class=\"p-2.5 border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/50 rounded-lg space-y-1.5 text-[11px]\">\n    <span class=\"font-bold text-white block\">Key Audit & Accounting Verification Points:</span>\n    <ul class=\"list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-slate-300\">\n      <li><span class=\"font-bold text-white\">Schedule 12 Disclosure:</span> Unexpired BGs and open LCs must be disclosed as <span class=\"font-bold text-amber-300\">Contingent Liabilities</span> under Schedule 12 of the Balance Sheet.</li>\n      <li><span class=\"font-bold text-white\">Margin Money Verification:</span> Ensure cash margin / term deposits are marked with a bank lien, held in separate accounts, and not freely withdrawable.</li>\n      <li><span class=\"font-bold text-white\">Devolvement Accounting:</span> If an LC is devolved or BG is invoked, bank pays the beneficiary and immediately debits the borrower's account.</li>\n      <li><span class=\"font-bold text-rose-400\">Immediate NPA Risk:</span> A devolved LC/invoked BG not regularized within 90 days renders the entire borrowing relationship an NPA.</li>\n    </ul>\n  </div>\n</div>\n",
    "summaryClean": "BGs and LCs are disclosed in Schedule 12; margins must be lien-marked; devolved facilities debit borrower accounts and trigger NPA if unpaid for 90 days."
